01:24:56.218 --> 01:24:58.038
I feel like no one in my school

01:24:58.038 --> 01:25:00.818
went anywhere foreign and like
studied there and came back.

01:25:00.818 --> 01:25:01.651
- Well, that's because,

01:25:01.651 --> 01:25:04.523
were there any Asian
people in your school?

01:25:04.523 --> 01:25:06.963
- One Asian person came to
my school, as I was leaving.

01:25:06.963 --> 01:25:08.741
(all laughing)

01:25:08.741 --> 01:25:09.654
I wish I was joking.

01:25:09.654 --> 01:25:11.646
I literally grew up in, like,

01:25:11.646 --> 01:25:13.936
the whitest part of the whole country.

01:25:13.936 --> 01:25:17.562
And, like, there was, like,
never any foreign people.

01:25:17.562 --> 01:25:18.425
- I was only, like,

01:25:18.425 --> 01:25:22.118
one of two Asian kids in
my whole school career.

01:25:22.118 --> 01:25:24.053
- I was the only one for my school.

01:25:24.053 --> 01:25:24.945
- I was the only one, as well.

01:25:24.945 --> 01:25:26.123
And, like, I grew up in Brighton,

01:25:26.123 --> 01:25:28.535
which is now seen as, like,
the very progressive city.

01:25:28.535 --> 01:25:30.317
- Ah, it's like the gay capitol of the UK.

01:25:30.317 --> 01:25:31.275
- Yeah, it was the gay capitol.

01:25:31.275 --> 01:25:32.108
I don't know if it still is,

01:25:32.108 --> 01:25:36.046
but now it's seen as the very
progressive city in England.

01:25:36.046 --> 01:25:37.966
But it wasn't like that
when I was growing up,

01:25:37.966 --> 01:25:38.799
I'll tell you that.

01:25:38.799 --> 01:25:41.983
Because I was literally the
only Asian person in my school.

01:25:41.983 --> 01:25:43.286
And my school wasn't small.

01:25:43.286 --> 01:25:46.464
We had, like, in sixth form,
we had, like 800 people or so.

01:25:46.464 --> 01:25:47.297
- [Joey] Fuckin' hell.
- Yeah, yeah.

01:25:47.297 --> 01:25:50.153
My graduating class had,
like, 600 something people.

01:25:50.153 --> 01:25:52.606
By high school there were a few more,

01:25:52.606 --> 01:25:53.624
but, like, middle school?

01:25:53.624 --> 01:25:54.457
Elementary school?

01:25:54.457 --> 01:25:55.337
Like, I--

01:25:55.337 --> 01:25:57.354
I'm sorry, secondary school?

01:25:57.354 --> 01:25:58.912
Or primary school?

01:25:58.912 --> 01:26:00.166
- I get confused about this shit.

01:26:00.166 --> 01:26:01.892
- I get confused, as well.
- I'm sorry, friends!

01:26:01.892 --> 01:26:02.754
- We say secondary school.

01:26:02.754 --> 01:26:04.554
- We say secondary school, but, like,

01:26:04.554 --> 01:26:05.703
I just call it high school now.

01:26:05.703 --> 01:26:06.676
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

01:26:06.676 --> 01:26:07.603
- It's easier, yeah.

01:26:07.603 --> 01:26:09.375
- We've been adopted by American culture.

01:26:09.375 --> 01:26:14.375
- But yeah, I don't know, it
wasn't really weird for me.

01:26:14.695 --> 01:26:18.744
I knew I got to step into a
different world every summer.

01:26:18.744 --> 01:26:20.515
And also, like, I love my family.

01:26:20.515 --> 01:26:24.645
And because my mom was able
to bring me back every year,

01:26:24.645 --> 01:26:26.436
it kind of stayed tethered.

01:26:26.436 --> 01:26:27.269
- Bring you back? (laughing)

01:26:27.269 --> 01:26:29.273
Like, "Sorry! Didn't
get the plane tickets!"

01:26:29.273 --> 01:26:30.354
(all laughing)

01:26:30.354 --> 01:26:32.102
- Just hoist me.

01:26:32.102 --> 01:26:34.348
Yeah, like, I don't know.

01:26:34.348 --> 01:26:37.796
I felt very connected, so it
wasn't that stark of a thing.

01:26:37.796 --> 01:26:39.567
Like, it was just a thing for me, right?

01:26:39.567 --> 01:26:40.565
Like, "Oh, every summer I go to Japan."

01:26:40.565 --> 01:26:41.775
Like, "Every winter I got to Japan."

01:26:41.775 --> 01:26:44.277
Maybe it's because I also
went two times a year

01:26:44.277 --> 01:26:46.043
that's also why I didn't feel--

01:26:46.043 --> 01:26:47.037
- I only got to go one time.

01:26:47.037 --> 01:26:48.826
- You are lucky, though, we
weren't in the same class.

01:26:48.826 --> 01:26:49.659
I would've been like,

01:26:49.659 --> 01:26:50.605
"Reina, Reina, fucking tell me everything!

01:26:50.605 --> 01:26:51.937
"How do they go? What do you do?"

01:26:51.937 --> 01:26:53.603
- Really? You'd be into Japan

01:26:53.603 --> 01:26:55.335
- Dude, I was! Yeah, as a kid!
- As a young child?

01:26:55.335 --> 01:26:56.576
- Yeah, I was, yeah, always.

01:26:56.576 --> 01:26:57.925
I mean, I guess that's why I'm
here right now, apparently.

01:26:57.925 --> 01:26:58.942
(all laughing)

01:26:58.942 --> 01:26:59.775
- I guess it is!

01:26:59.775 --> 01:27:01.763
- Ever since a kid, I always just thought

01:27:01.763 --> 01:27:03.241
Asia was super cool and, like,

01:27:03.241 --> 01:27:06.001
to Europe, it's the
furthest place from you.

01:27:06.001 --> 01:27:07.034
- Which is funny, right?

01:27:07.034 --> 01:27:08.277
Because people in Asia are like,

01:27:08.277 --> 01:27:09.429
"Oh, man, Europe is so cool."

01:27:09.429 --> 01:27:10.717
- "Aw, Europe is amazing!"

01:27:10.717 --> 01:27:12.500
- Now, I really like Europe.

01:27:12.500 --> 01:27:13.347
But when I was growing up, I was like,

01:27:13.347 --> 01:27:14.526
"Mum, I don't want to
go to fucking Romania.

01:27:14.526 --> 01:27:16.686
"I don't want to go to
Bulgaria." Or whatever.

01:27:16.686 --> 01:27:18.939
Like, "Take me to Asia!"

01:27:18.939 --> 01:27:20.868
'Cause it all fucking
looks the same in Europe.

01:27:20.868 --> 01:27:23.195
It doesn't, but as a kid,
it all feels the same.

01:27:23.195 --> 01:27:24.368
(group agreeing)

01:27:24.368 --> 01:27:28.735
- I remember when I was,
like, maybe 12 or something.

01:27:28.735 --> 01:27:32.707
We were shown "Big Bird Goes To Japan"

01:27:32.707 --> 01:27:34.739
in one of our history classes.

01:27:34.739 --> 01:27:35.627
- Oh, no.

01:27:35.627 --> 01:27:40.024
- And "one, two, three is
ichi, ni, san" was really huge.

01:27:40.024 --> 01:27:41.847
And then everybody came
to me, all the sudden,

01:27:41.847 --> 01:27:44.804
and they were like,
"Do you have a kimono?"

01:27:44.804 --> 01:27:45.883
(guys laughing)

01:27:45.883 --> 01:27:48.545
And, like, "Do you pay in yern?"

01:27:48.545 --> 01:27:49.645
Like, they didn't know what the fuck.

01:27:49.645 --> 01:27:50.534
- [Guys] Yern?!

01:27:50.534 --> 01:27:51.481
(all laughing)

01:27:51.481 --> 01:27:52.314
- Yern!

01:27:52.314 --> 01:27:54.054
- Like, that was, I
think, the first, like,

01:27:54.054 --> 01:27:55.834
super fascination that people had.

01:27:55.834 --> 01:27:59.312
And I was like, "Really? A
big bird, literal Big Bird,

01:27:59.312 --> 01:28:01.026
"made you interested in Japan?"

01:28:01.026 --> 01:28:02.824
And they're like, "Really, Ohio?"

01:28:02.824 --> 01:28:04.085
Which is a state in the US,

01:28:04.085 --> 01:28:06.175
"Ohio means good morning?"

01:28:06.175 --> 01:28:07.894
And I'm like, "Yes, fuck."

01:28:07.894 --> 01:28:09.844
Like, "Yeah, we speak a different

01:28:09.844 --> 01:28:13.396
"fucking language than you, bro!"

01:28:13.396 --> 01:28:14.739
But yeah, so, that was my experience

01:28:14.739 --> 01:28:16.097
growing up, like, foreign.

01:28:16.097 --> 01:28:18.170
- So, there wasn't like kids
who were into the culture

01:28:18.170 --> 01:28:19.997
that were like, "Reina, Reina
I gotta ask you things."?

01:28:19.997 --> 01:28:24.590
- You know, I had a parent
that was very into Japan.

01:28:24.590 --> 01:28:26.590
- Oh, no. That kind of sounds weird.

01:28:26.590 --> 01:28:28.500
- Yeah, and, like, she'd really want

01:28:28.500 --> 01:28:30.865
her daughter to be friends with
me, because she loved Japan.

01:28:30.865 --> 01:28:32.683
(group groaning)

01:28:32.683 --> 01:28:35.280
And she, like, always wanted
to have tea with my mom.

01:28:35.280 --> 01:28:36.495
Um, green tea.

01:28:36.495 --> 01:28:38.324
(all laughing)

01:28:38.324 --> 01:28:39.157
- Of course.

01:28:39.157 --> 01:28:40.144
That's all we drink.

01:28:40.144 --> 01:28:41.945
- Yeah, she was like, "Matcha!"

01:28:41.945 --> 01:28:45.424
But, yeah, that was like the only

01:28:45.424 --> 01:28:48.111
hyper-concentrated interest,
I think anybody had.

01:28:48.111 --> 01:28:50.284
I did not care for this girl.

01:28:50.284 --> 01:28:52.527
(guys laughing)

01:28:52.527 --> 01:28:53.610
- Yeah, it sucked 'cause I always wanted

01:28:53.610 --> 01:28:54.443
to learn more about it,

01:28:54.443 --> 01:28:56.057
but you were just so limited
on what you could find.

01:28:56.057 --> 01:28:56.890
'Cause I didn't know anyone.

01:28:56.890 --> 01:28:57.723
- Other than the internet, right?

01:28:57.723 --> 01:28:58.965
- I didn't know anyone who knew anyone.

01:28:58.965 --> 01:29:00.193
- Even through the internet, as well,

01:29:00.193 --> 01:29:01.966
it all came from, like,
second, third hand accounts.

01:29:01.966 --> 01:29:03.737
So, no one was actually,
like, documenting it.

01:29:03.737 --> 01:29:07.301
- Right, you can't get
to like really know.

01:29:07.301 --> 01:29:08.713
- So, you just have to, like, read forums

01:29:08.713 --> 01:29:10.526
and have to, like, piece things together.

01:29:10.526 --> 01:29:11.675
- Like, "I think this is correct."

01:29:11.675 --> 01:29:14.511
- "I think this is the right
thing, I'm not really sure.

01:29:14.511 --> 01:29:16.273
"but I'll ask, I'll look around."

01:29:16.273 --> 01:29:18.096
'Cause, you know, I always
just loved games, as well.

01:29:18.096 --> 01:29:20.062
And games are like a huge
thing to why I was like,

01:29:20.062 --> 01:29:21.142
"Where do these games come from?"

01:29:21.142 --> 01:29:24.554
- Yeah, so, gaming was
the other thing, I think,

01:29:24.554 --> 01:29:26.594
that brought attention to my nationality.

01:29:26.594 --> 01:29:30.384
When DDR came, everyone's
like, "Wow, Japan!"

01:29:30.384 --> 01:29:34.894
Like, "Can you sing
'Butterfly' or, like, 'Candy?'"

01:29:34.894 --> 01:29:36.692
That was it, that was the biggest.

01:29:36.692 --> 01:29:37.580
- That's horrifying.

01:29:37.580 --> 01:29:38.413
- I know! I know.

01:29:38.413 --> 01:29:40.071
- Were you into DDR, though?

01:29:40.071 --> 01:29:40.904
- I loved DDR.

01:29:40.904 --> 01:29:41.839
(all laughing)

01:29:41.839 --> 01:29:42.919
- That probably didn't help, then.

01:29:42.919 --> 01:29:44.070
- It didn't help, it didn't help.

01:29:44.070 --> 01:29:45.214
- Just reinforcing the stereotype.

01:29:45.214 --> 01:29:48.139
- You're like, "God, fine,
I'll spit fire, geez."

01:29:48.139 --> 01:29:50.344
- I mean, like, fuck,

01:29:50.344 --> 01:29:53.427
- Do you eat sushi every day?

01:29:53.427 --> 01:29:54.421
Oh my god.

01:29:54.421 --> 01:29:55.951
- Oh yeah, I guess, actually,

01:29:55.951 --> 01:29:57.912
food was a little bit of a deal.

01:29:57.912 --> 01:30:00.129
Ramen wasn't that big
back then, but like sushi.

01:30:00.129 --> 01:30:00.962
- It's big now, right?

01:30:00.962 --> 01:30:01.795
- Oh, huge.

01:30:01.795 --> 01:30:02.957
- I mean, Japanese cuisine,

01:30:02.957 --> 01:30:04.710
I feel, like, exploded during my lifetime.

01:30:04.710 --> 01:30:06.496
It wasn't that big when I was growing up,

01:30:06.496 --> 01:30:07.329
but now it's like--

01:30:07.329 --> 01:30:08.228
- In the UK, do you think so?

01:30:08.228 --> 01:30:10.755
I feel like we still only really
have like sushi in the UK.

01:30:10.755 --> 01:30:11.888
- Not even ramen?

01:30:11.888 --> 01:30:13.275
- There's the occasional ramen place,

01:30:13.275 --> 01:30:16.018
but nothing like worth
getting super excited over.

01:30:16.018 --> 01:30:18.738
- The US has completely taken that over.

01:30:18.738 --> 01:30:19.571
- Ramen's everywhere now!

01:30:19.571 --> 01:30:20.404
- Everywhere now.

01:30:20.404 --> 01:30:21.411
- Yeah, but there wasn't
a single ramen restaurant

01:30:21.411 --> 01:30:24.144
in America where I'm like, "This is good."

01:30:24.144 --> 01:30:24.977
- Yeah, me neither.

01:30:24.977 --> 01:30:26.763
- To be fair, it would be hard, right?

01:30:26.763 --> 01:30:30.060
- Although, to be fair, in
Vegas, I did go to a place,

01:30:30.060 --> 01:30:33.156
a ramen place, which
dead-ass was called Naruto.

01:30:33.156 --> 01:30:35.357
(all laughing)

01:30:35.357 --> 01:30:36.373
- That gets points just for that.

01:30:36.373 --> 01:30:37.920
- Straight up, and I was like,

01:30:37.920 --> 01:30:39.771
"Aki, why are we not
eating there every day?"

01:30:39.771 --> 01:30:41.672
Fuckin' amazing.

01:30:41.672 --> 01:30:43.414
- I became so picky with ramen here.

01:30:43.414 --> 01:30:44.521
- You should. As you should.

01:30:44.521 --> 01:30:46.363
- It's so easy to fuck
up, I didn't realize.

01:30:46.363 --> 01:30:47.280
- [Joey] It really is.

01:30:47.280 --> 01:30:48.153
- You know, when you're not here,

01:30:48.153 --> 01:30:48.986
and you're not eating the ramen here,

01:30:48.986 --> 01:30:50.758
you're like, "Oh yeah,
it's ramen same thing."

01:30:50.758 --> 01:30:52.191
But then when you come here, you're like,

01:30:52.191 --> 01:30:54.810
"Broth is 4% too salty.

01:30:54.810 --> 01:30:56.850
"The noodles were slightly undercooked,

01:30:56.850 --> 01:30:58.891
"this is really embarrassing
for you, this is your job."

01:30:58.891 --> 01:31:00.850
- You just become, like, an
absolute fucking food snob

01:31:00.850 --> 01:31:01.910
when you live here long enough.

01:31:01.910 --> 01:31:02.969
(group agreeing)

01:31:02.969 --> 01:31:05.168
I never used to give a shit
about, like, the type of ramen.

01:31:05.168 --> 01:31:06.159
Or the type of sushi.

01:31:06.159 --> 01:31:07.704
But now, I'm like,

01:31:07.704 --> 01:31:12.102
"No, no, I only eat at one
specific sushi train franchise."

01:31:12.102 --> 01:31:15.365
"Anywhere else, 100 yen sushi?
Get that shit out of here."

01:31:15.365 --> 01:31:17.149
- So many of them fuck up the pork.

01:31:17.149 --> 01:31:20.205
Like, it's so, like, old and, like, tough.

01:31:20.205 --> 01:31:21.038
And I'm like, "What did
you do to this pork?"

01:31:21.038 --> 01:31:21.871
- Oh, the slices?

01:31:21.871 --> 01:31:23.884
- It has to be like, perfect texture

01:31:23.884 --> 01:31:25.296
that just, like, kind of
falls apart in your mouth.

01:31:25.296 --> 01:31:26.477
(all agreeing)

01:31:26.477 --> 01:31:28.735
Yeah, like, I find myself eating ramen

01:31:28.735 --> 01:31:30.791
a lot less in Japan
than I thought I would.

01:31:30.791 --> 01:31:33.980
Like, sushi fuckin' slaps
here, I could eat that any day.

01:31:33.980 --> 01:31:36.291
- Also ramen takes you out
of business for the day.

01:31:36.291 --> 01:31:37.260
- Yeah!

01:31:37.260 --> 01:31:38.749
- Like, you can't do
anything if you eat ramen.

01:31:38.749 --> 01:31:40.459
- It's so heavy and it's so bad for you!

01:31:40.459 --> 01:31:42.100
Like, it's delicious, but, like, it's--

01:31:42.100 --> 01:31:43.411
- It is extremely bad for you.

01:31:43.411 --> 01:31:44.918
- It's really bad for you!

01:31:44.918 --> 01:31:47.100
And, like, you're not supposed
to drink the whole broth.

01:31:47.100 --> 01:31:48.293
That's the killer.

01:31:48.293 --> 01:31:49.288
- Fuck.

01:31:49.288 --> 01:31:51.387
- Sorry, I knew. I looked
at you for a reason,

01:31:51.387 --> 01:31:52.341
like, I knew you would.

01:31:52.341 --> 01:31:53.650
- You're like, "White
guy, of course he did."

01:31:53.650 --> 01:31:55.536
(group laughing) Dude, because
when I go anywhere, I'm like,

01:31:55.536 --> 01:31:57.723
"I don't want to feel like
I'm leaving anything."

01:31:57.723 --> 01:31:58.575
'Cause I feel rude.

01:31:58.575 --> 01:32:00.735
So, I'm like, I look at the guy making it,

01:32:00.735 --> 01:32:01.913
I'm like, "All right, fuck, okay."

01:32:01.913 --> 01:32:02.746
- Take it all in!

01:32:02.746 --> 01:32:03.682
- Chug, chug.

01:32:03.682 --> 01:32:04.804
(group laughing)

01:32:04.804 --> 01:32:07.405
- I guess I could just
drink the fucking Dead Sea.

01:32:07.405 --> 01:32:11.285
- But, to be fair, okay yes,
the sodium is through the roof.

01:32:11.285 --> 01:32:12.120
But sometimes, some of the bowls

01:32:12.120 --> 01:32:13.303
have like the thank you
message at the bottom

01:32:13.303 --> 01:32:14.575
if you drink it all.

01:32:14.575 --> 01:32:15.606
- Is that what you're going for?

01:32:15.606 --> 01:32:16.490
- That's how they get you!

01:32:16.490 --> 01:32:17.531
That's how they literally get you.

01:32:17.531 --> 01:32:19.409
- Because I want to see
the thank you message!

01:32:19.409 --> 01:32:21.809
- But most of the time there
isn't and do you get sad?

01:32:21.809 --> 01:32:24.430
- Yeah, actually, I get real fucking sad.

01:32:24.430 --> 01:32:25.432
- I did it for nothing!

01:32:25.432 --> 01:32:26.919
- I drink, like, a liter of this--

01:32:26.919 --> 01:32:27.768
- Salt.

01:32:27.768 --> 01:32:29.819
- I feel awful all day,
I have to like lie down.

01:32:29.819 --> 01:32:31.768
And then I didn't even get a thank you.

01:32:31.768 --> 01:32:33.126
- The bowl didn't thank you.

01:32:33.126 --> 01:32:34.667
- I like to think the guy is like,

01:32:34.667 --> 01:32:36.719
"Nice guy, he made my life a
little easier, he cleaned it."

01:32:36.719 --> 01:32:37.968
But he probably doesn't give a fuck.

01:32:37.968 --> 01:32:38.920
- He doesn't give a fuck!

01:32:38.920 --> 01:32:41.517
- He gets the pressure washer
and just (wooshing sounds)

01:32:41.517 --> 01:32:42.350
and then it's, like, clean.

01:32:42.350 --> 01:32:43.767
Huh, there we go.

01:32:44.683 --> 01:32:47.878
- Yeah, ramen, you definitely
get picky in Japan.

01:32:47.878 --> 01:32:50.399
But that's also because, you know,

01:32:50.399 --> 01:32:53.029
there's a lot of factors to it, right?

01:32:53.029 --> 01:32:54.668
Is the noodle too chewy?

01:32:54.668 --> 01:32:56.570
Is the broth too fatty?

01:32:56.570 --> 01:32:57.926
But it's also, like, personal.

01:32:57.926 --> 01:33:01.359
- Also, sometimes, you get like rushed.

01:33:01.359 --> 01:33:03.028
And when it's super busy--
- Oh, you do get rushed.

01:33:03.028 --> 01:33:05.398
Oh yeah, I didn't think about that.

01:33:05.398 --> 01:33:07.527
- All the famous ramen places
in Tokyo always have lines.

01:33:07.527 --> 01:33:10.193
And you're expected to eat
it and get the fuck out.

01:33:10.193 --> 01:33:11.093
You can't go with friends,

01:33:11.093 --> 01:33:12.466
'cause that's not really what it's for.

01:33:12.466 --> 01:33:14.437
'Cause there's not gonna
be like three seats empty.

01:33:14.437 --> 01:33:15.589
- Well, I know you guys have, like,

01:33:15.589 --> 01:33:18.848
constantly told me how
fucking fast I eat my ramen.

01:33:18.848 --> 01:33:20.209
- That's a skill.

01:33:20.209 --> 01:33:21.610
- It's literally just
I've been conditioned

01:33:21.610 --> 01:33:22.443
to eat it that way.

01:33:22.443 --> 01:33:25.055
- Joey fucking vacuums
his ramen, I swear to god.

01:33:25.055 --> 01:33:26.306
- I'm normally the one
who eats super fast,

01:33:26.306 --> 01:33:28.122
and then it's really weird being with Joey

01:33:28.122 --> 01:33:29.431
where he just destroys the
ramen. Like, wait, hold up.

01:33:29.431 --> 01:33:31.991
- Yeah, well, it's because, like,

01:33:31.991 --> 01:33:33.281
when I was still visiting here

01:33:33.281 --> 01:33:34.984
and my uncle would take me to, like,

01:33:34.984 --> 01:33:37.431
the best fucking, like,
ramen and tsukemen places.

01:33:37.431 --> 01:33:38.431
- He's like, "We're leaving.
We're leaving right now."

01:33:38.431 --> 01:33:39.264
- It's always like that!

01:33:39.264 --> 01:33:40.648
It's always like,

01:33:40.648 --> 01:33:43.061
"This stall can only hold like
three people sitting down."

01:33:43.061 --> 01:33:45.490
So, it's like, there's always, like,

01:33:45.490 --> 01:33:46.323
20 people waiting outside.

01:33:46.323 --> 01:33:48.248
So, it's like, if you dilly dally in here,

01:33:48.248 --> 01:33:49.780
you're not going to be welcome back.

01:33:49.780 --> 01:33:51.446
(all agreeing)
- Yeah, 'cause you can't talk

01:33:51.446 --> 01:33:53.019
with your friends when you go in there.

01:33:53.019 --> 01:33:54.029
- No, no, no, you have to concentrate.

01:33:54.029 --> 01:33:56.442
And actually, it is a skill
to eat ramen real fast.

01:33:56.442 --> 01:33:57.275
I eat really fast too,
it like scares people.

01:33:57.275 --> 01:34:00.523
But, you know that slurping
that you're supposed to do?

01:34:00.523 --> 01:34:02.425
That's like a purposeful thing.

01:34:02.425 --> 01:34:03.892
- Yeah, it cools it down, right?

01:34:03.892 --> 01:34:04.959
- Yeah! So you can just
eat the whole thing

01:34:04.959 --> 01:34:06.573
while it's piping hot.

01:34:06.573 --> 01:34:08.054
Which is, like, a really strange--

01:34:08.054 --> 01:34:11.673
you're not, weirdly, there to enjoy it.

01:34:11.673 --> 01:34:13.100
- Yeah, it's there for a purpose.

01:34:13.100 --> 01:34:14.179
- You consume it.

01:34:14.179 --> 01:34:16.581
- Sort of like, "Fill my
stomach, get the fuck out."

01:34:16.581 --> 01:34:18.061
- Yeah, but there's some places,

01:34:18.061 --> 01:34:19.011
the ramen is so good that you're like,

01:34:19.011 --> 01:34:21.144
"I need to take my time."

01:34:21.144 --> 01:34:21.977
- I know!

01:34:21.977 --> 01:34:23.344
(whispers) But you're not supposed to.

01:34:23.344 --> 01:34:24.177
I'm just kidding.

01:34:24.177 --> 01:34:25.573
- Which is why I'll try and go

01:34:25.573 --> 01:34:27.906
at like awkward times, like 3PM.

01:34:27.906 --> 01:34:30.185
'Cause normally there's never a line,

01:34:30.185 --> 01:34:33.572
no one's coming for dinner,
no one's going for lunch.

01:34:33.572 --> 01:34:37.432
But then you've fucked up your
eating schedule for the day.

01:34:37.432 --> 01:34:39.431
- Right. I always feel so ungraceful

01:34:39.431 --> 01:34:40.334
getting out of the stools.

01:34:40.334 --> 01:34:42.943
I'm like, "I look like
I'm two months pregnant."

01:34:42.943 --> 01:34:45.883
And I gotta like wedge my way out of here.

01:34:45.883 --> 01:34:47.026
- Like, you can the soup just

01:34:47.026 --> 01:34:49.982
swishing around in your stomach.

01:34:49.982 --> 01:34:50.815
(group agreeing)

01:34:50.815 --> 01:34:51.876
- You gotta like move it over.

01:34:51.876 --> 01:34:53.402
- The worst is, if you're
getting on the train afterwards,

01:34:53.402 --> 01:34:54.563
the moment you sit down on the train,

01:34:54.563 --> 01:34:57.337
it's like sleep is activated.

01:34:57.337 --> 01:34:59.155
- It does rock you to
sleep, it really does.

01:34:59.155 --> 01:35:00.446
That food coma is real.

01:35:00.446 --> 01:35:01.637
- But it's so good!

01:35:01.637 --> 01:35:02.470
Go eat it.

01:35:02.470 --> 01:35:03.303
(all laughing)

01:35:03.303 --> 01:35:04.450
- Just don't go to Ichiran, right?

01:35:04.450 --> 01:35:06.898
- I like Ichiran, Ichiran's good.

01:35:06.898 --> 01:35:08.887
- I remember when you took
me there for the first time,

01:35:08.887 --> 01:35:10.054
'cause I'd never been to Ichiran,

01:35:10.054 --> 01:35:11.533
'cause I'd only been
to, like, local places.

01:35:11.533 --> 01:35:15.357
So, I think it was the day
after our medical exam,

01:35:15.357 --> 01:35:17.302
and Connor's like, "Guys,
we're gonna go to Ichiran."

01:35:17.302 --> 01:35:20.527
- Well, no, I wanted to
get fucked up by ramen.

01:35:20.527 --> 01:35:21.900
- Fucked up by ramen!

01:35:21.900 --> 01:35:22.770
- Let's get fucked!

01:35:22.770 --> 01:35:24.226
- So, we weren't allowed to eat before.

01:35:24.226 --> 01:35:27.057
We weren't allowed to eat from
like 8PM the night before.

01:35:27.057 --> 01:35:29.046
Which doesn't sound bad, but
when you're told you can't eat

01:35:29.046 --> 01:35:29.879
- Oh yeah, it hurts.

01:35:29.879 --> 01:35:31.745
- Then you're like, "Now
I'm hungry." (all agreeing)

01:35:31.745 --> 01:35:33.217
- I remember we were eating
it, and Connor was like,

01:35:33.217 --> 01:35:34.604
"Go on, how is it? How is it?"

01:35:34.604 --> 01:35:36.505
And I'd never had such a hard time

01:35:36.505 --> 01:35:39.164
forming an opinion until that moment.

01:35:39.164 --> 01:35:43.462
- Ichiran is the most
solid five out of ten.

01:35:43.462 --> 01:35:45.543
- The thing I like about it
- That's it, that's it.

01:35:45.543 --> 01:35:46.955
- Ichiran is a chain of
ramen that's seen as, like,

01:35:46.955 --> 01:35:48.138
very touristy, I guess.

01:35:48.138 --> 01:35:50.047
The one thing I do like about
it though, is that you can,

01:35:50.047 --> 01:35:52.576
I know this isn't a thing for ramen,

01:35:52.576 --> 01:35:53.737
you're not supposed to do this,

01:35:53.737 --> 01:35:55.327
you can customize the spice level.

01:35:55.327 --> 01:35:56.575
(group agreeing)

01:35:56.575 --> 01:35:57.996
I really like spicy ramen,

01:35:57.996 --> 01:35:59.762
and nowhere ever does spicy ramen.

01:35:59.762 --> 01:36:01.644
So, it's nice that you can be like,

01:36:01.644 --> 01:36:04.924
"Hey, but a habanero in
this shit." And they do.

01:36:04.924 --> 01:36:07.627
And then you can order, like,
extra meat, extra noodles,

01:36:07.627 --> 01:36:08.961
like, it's all chill.

01:36:08.961 --> 01:36:10.544
- The customization is fun, yeah.

01:36:10.544 --> 01:36:13.058
- The customization is
what gets the tourists.

01:36:13.058 --> 01:36:14.437
- It's not the best by any means,

01:36:14.437 --> 01:36:15.871
but it's like the most comfortable.

01:36:15.871 --> 01:36:16.979
- I like it.

01:36:16.979 --> 01:36:21.856
I know that I won't, like,
a two if I got there, right?

01:36:21.856 --> 01:36:22.689
Like, a solid five.

01:36:22.689 --> 01:36:24.799
Like, I know I won't completely fuck up.

01:36:24.799 --> 01:36:26.038
- It was just like a solid five.

01:36:26.038 --> 01:36:30.650
And I'm just like, "Well, that
was a meal that I consumed.

01:36:30.650 --> 01:36:34.449
"And it wasn't bad and it did the job.

01:36:34.449 --> 01:36:36.847
"I am now full, thank you very much."

01:36:36.847 --> 01:36:39.673
- Like if you wrote an
IGN review for Ichiran,

01:36:39.673 --> 01:36:42.456
it'd just be like,
"Good. Five out of ten."

01:36:42.456 --> 01:36:43.289
(group laughing)

01:36:43.289 --> 01:36:44.375
There's like nothing else
you can say about it!

01:36:44.375 --> 01:36:45.925
- You should go to
Ichiran, it's pretty good.

01:36:45.925 --> 01:36:46.973
Check it out.

01:36:46.973 --> 01:36:50.049
You should go there first as a baseline.

01:36:50.049 --> 01:36:51.575
- Oh, that's actually a really good idea.

01:36:51.575 --> 01:36:52.408
- [Joey] I agree.

01:36:52.408 --> 01:36:53.346
- And they're all over Shinjuku,

01:36:53.346 --> 01:36:55.305
there's like three right
next to the station.

01:36:55.305 --> 01:36:56.138
- Oh, are there?

01:36:56.138 --> 01:36:57.224
- Yeah.
- Ugh.

01:36:57.224 --> 01:36:58.264
- All in the sketchy parts.

01:36:58.264 --> 01:37:01.177
When we left that Ichiran,
we literally walked out

01:37:01.177 --> 01:37:02.638
and a guy came up to us, he
was like, "You want sex?"

01:37:02.638 --> 01:37:03.847
"You want sex?"

01:37:03.847 --> 01:37:04.986
And we're, like, literally
in front of the station,

01:37:04.986 --> 01:37:06.166
I'm like, "What is happening?"

01:37:06.166 --> 01:37:08.361
- It wasn't, like, even late at night.

01:37:08.361 --> 01:37:09.229
- It was, like, mid-day!

01:37:09.229 --> 01:37:10.062
- It was mid-day!

01:37:10.062 --> 01:37:12.013
It was literally lunch time.

01:37:12.013 --> 01:37:14.086
- Like, "Do you want
lunch? Do you want lunch?"

01:37:14.086 --> 01:37:16.017
- He said it in English?

01:37:16.017 --> 01:37:17.788
- Yeah, it's 'cause you're foreign.

01:37:17.788 --> 01:37:20.371
They don't bug Japanese people.

01:37:20.371 --> 01:37:21.552
- Yeah.

01:37:21.552 --> 01:37:24.520
- I remember, I asked this
to one of the bar owners

01:37:24.520 --> 01:37:26.378
around the area. I was like,
"Why did they only, like,

01:37:26.378 --> 01:37:27.529
"come up to foreigners?"

01:37:27.529 --> 01:37:28.479
And they're like, "Oh,
'cause Japanese people

01:37:28.479 --> 01:37:29.660
"will call the police."

01:37:29.660 --> 01:37:30.577
- Oh, really?

01:37:30.577 --> 01:37:31.498
- Really?

01:37:31.498 --> 01:37:33.680
- 'Cause the dudes will come up to you--

01:37:33.680 --> 01:37:35.219
- I guess it is sexual assault.

01:37:35.219 --> 01:37:36.858
- Yeah, they'll put their arms around you,

01:37:36.858 --> 01:37:37.971
like, "Hey, where you wanna go?

01:37:37.971 --> 01:37:38.823
"You looking for some good time?"

01:37:38.823 --> 01:37:40.181
And it's like, "Leave me the fuck alone."

01:37:40.181 --> 01:37:41.287
- Ugh.

01:37:41.287 --> 01:37:43.245
- I can see the Japanese
calling the police for that.

01:37:43.245 --> 01:37:45.210
- Yeah, if I a guy puts
his arm around you,

01:37:45.210 --> 01:37:46.053
they're not gonna do it.

01:37:46.053 --> 01:37:47.484
And they know the Japanese
aren't gonna talk to them.

01:37:47.484 --> 01:37:48.317
'Cause they're terrifying,
I mean, they are.

01:37:48.317 --> 01:37:49.582
'Cause they just come up to you

01:37:49.582 --> 01:37:52.953
and they're quite intimidating,
they're like pretty upfront.

01:37:52.953 --> 01:37:55.956
- "Hi sir, you look different
from everyone else here."

01:37:55.956 --> 01:37:56.856
"What are you doing?"

01:37:56.856 --> 01:37:58.392
- Yeah, it's fine though.

01:37:58.392 --> 01:37:59.796
It is what it is, deal with it.

01:37:59.796 --> 01:38:00.731
- Damn.

01:38:00.731 --> 01:38:02.835
- So, like, going back to
your experiences in school

01:38:02.835 --> 01:38:03.912
and everything, with being Japanese,

01:38:03.912 --> 01:38:07.116
were you ever open about watching anime

01:38:07.116 --> 01:38:08.716
or did you ever get bullied for that?

01:38:08.716 --> 01:38:11.216
- Ooh, um, in American school,

01:38:12.374 --> 01:38:15.186
I don't think I ever really brought it up.

01:38:15.186 --> 01:38:17.308
It's not like I was trying
to keep it a secret.

01:38:17.308 --> 01:38:19.525
- It doesn't come up in conversation.

01:38:19.525 --> 01:38:22.256
- Right, right, and I wasn't
like, "These are my interests."

01:38:22.256 --> 01:38:26.706
But, oh god, I do remember
something weird did happen.

01:38:26.706 --> 01:38:30.684
I had to do a book report
and an autobiography.

01:38:30.684 --> 01:38:33.016
And I did it on Sir Arthur Conan Doyle

01:38:33.016 --> 01:38:35.667
because I actually, really
do like Sherlock Holmes.

01:38:35.667 --> 01:38:36.500
But, I also--

01:38:36.500 --> 01:38:37.632
- I already know where this is going.

01:38:37.632 --> 01:38:39.651
- I know, but I also like
Sherlock Holmes because

01:38:39.651 --> 01:38:43.197
my favorite anime of all
time is Detective Conan.

01:38:43.197 --> 01:38:44.030
(guys laughing)

01:38:44.030 --> 01:38:46.451
I grew with it, it's like my baby.

01:38:46.451 --> 01:38:47.741
It's older than me now.

01:38:47.741 --> 01:38:50.269
Like, it's crazy, but
I was obsessed with it.

01:38:50.269 --> 01:38:52.073
And all throughout my life, I loved it.

01:38:52.073 --> 01:38:54.929
And I loved it, so I
started reading, like,

01:38:54.929 --> 01:38:56.003
real Sherlock Holmes, you know?

01:38:56.003 --> 01:38:56.842
(group agreeing)

01:38:56.842 --> 01:38:57.675
And I was, like,

01:38:57.675 --> 01:38:58.534
"I'm gonna do my whole
book report on this."

01:38:58.534 --> 01:39:00.402
And I got like really into it.

01:39:00.402 --> 01:39:03.132
Like, it was, like, a
15 minute presentation.

01:39:03.132 --> 01:39:04.894
- They're like, "Reina, please stop."

01:39:04.894 --> 01:39:05.781
(group laughing)

01:39:05.781 --> 01:39:07.081
- Yeah, she was like,
"You already got the A."

01:39:07.081 --> 01:39:08.220
Like, "Shut the fuck up."

01:39:08.220 --> 01:39:09.111
(group laughing)

01:39:09.111 --> 01:39:11.053
Like, "Fuck, we get it,
you're, like, an Asian nerd."

01:39:11.053 --> 01:39:13.381
Like, "God damn, sit down."

01:39:13.381 --> 01:39:16.832
But that was when in
the whole presentation,

01:39:16.832 --> 01:39:19.905
towards the end, I started
talking about Detective Conan.

01:39:19.905 --> 01:39:20.831
(all laughing)

01:39:20.831 --> 01:39:24.340
I was like, I had to
explain something, like,

01:39:24.340 --> 01:39:25.633
about his name, right?

01:39:25.633 --> 01:39:27.275
And other iterations of his name.

01:39:27.275 --> 01:39:28.108
And I was like,

01:39:28.108 --> 01:39:30.223
"And in Japan, the most popular anime

01:39:30.223 --> 01:39:33.343
"is called, 'Detective Conan'
and it's about, you know,

01:39:33.343 --> 01:39:35.630
"Conan Doyle, but it's not."

01:39:35.630 --> 01:39:38.164
And I went on like a really nerdy tangent.

01:39:38.164 --> 01:39:40.621
- You literally did like
an anime analysis video of

01:39:40.621 --> 01:39:43.242
why Conan is called Edogawa Conan.

01:39:43.242 --> 01:39:44.752
- Yeah, I did! I did!

01:39:44.752 --> 01:39:48.752
Yeah, because Aoyama Gosho
uses different, like,

01:39:50.119 --> 01:39:53.682
specifically different
famous literature figures

01:39:53.682 --> 01:39:57.293
that are detective novelists
in his book jackets

01:39:57.293 --> 01:40:00.273
and they work their way into the anime!

01:40:00.273 --> 01:40:02.384
And I was like so excited about it!

01:40:02.384 --> 01:40:05.512
And like, Cordelia Gray is Haibara Ai,

01:40:05.512 --> 01:40:07.582
because "gray" is "ai."

01:40:07.582 --> 01:40:09.135
(group laughing)

01:40:09.135 --> 01:40:11.634
- It's a tough thing to learn
as a kid, when you're like,

01:40:11.634 --> 01:40:13.996
"Man, people don't care about
the things that I care about."

01:40:13.996 --> 01:40:15.334
(all laughing)

01:40:15.334 --> 01:40:17.424
- I mean, like, I was fine.

01:40:17.424 --> 01:40:18.733
I didn't get, like, bullied or anything.

01:40:18.733 --> 01:40:22.065
But that was when I was
like, "I gotta turn it down."

01:40:22.065 --> 01:40:23.264
(all laughing)

01:40:23.264 --> 01:40:25.422
- I'm weirding people out.

01:40:25.422 --> 01:40:27.535
- Yeah, like, I gotta shut up right now.

01:40:27.535 --> 01:40:29.353
- I got rinsed for
saying I liked One Piece

01:40:29.353 --> 01:40:30.625
when I was like 12.

01:40:30.625 --> 01:40:31.458
- What? Why?

01:40:31.458 --> 01:40:32.810
- Wait, but you've never even seen it.

01:40:32.810 --> 01:40:33.776
- No, I did, when I was a kid.

01:40:33.776 --> 01:40:34.609
- Oh, really?

01:40:34.609 --> 01:40:35.565
- Yeah, I watched the Four Kids version.

01:40:35.565 --> 01:40:37.419
- The Four Kids version!
- Oh, no!

01:40:37.419 --> 01:40:38.717
- Well then, I would've
bullied you too, for that.

01:40:38.717 --> 01:40:41.691
(all laughing)
- Yeah, they were just like,

01:40:41.691 --> 01:40:44.074
"Why are you watching cartoons,
Connor? We're 11, grow up."

01:40:44.074 --> 01:40:44.907
- Oh yeah.

01:40:46.079 --> 01:40:46.997
- My parents were like,

01:40:46.997 --> 01:40:49.075
"When are you gonna
stop watching cartoons?"

01:40:49.075 --> 01:40:50.387
And I'm, like, 13, I'm like,

01:40:50.387 --> 01:40:52.677
"Am I supposed to stop? What?
This is awesome though."

01:40:52.677 --> 01:40:54.565
- My parents kept telling
me, "You'll grow out of this.

01:40:54.565 --> 01:40:55.398
"You'll grow out of this."

01:40:55.398 --> 01:40:57.988
Here I am, like, about
to go to university,

01:40:57.988 --> 01:40:59.875
"Am I gonna grow out of this?

01:40:59.875 --> 01:41:01.997
"I'm still really
enjoying this right now."

01:41:01.997 --> 01:41:03.315
- Make a career out of it!

01:41:03.315 --> 01:41:05.635
- Was there a thing like that
in, like, American schools?

01:41:05.635 --> 01:41:06.831
Where it was like they
expect you to, like,

01:41:06.831 --> 01:41:09.086
stop talking about stuff like that?

01:41:09.086 --> 01:41:10.923
- You know, there definitely was.

01:41:10.923 --> 01:41:12.273
And I think I was also, like, a--

01:41:12.273 --> 01:41:14.655
I grew up in, like, you
know, late 90s, 2000,

01:41:14.655 --> 01:41:16.495
and there was definitely, kind of, like,

01:41:16.495 --> 01:41:18.344
a we want to pretend to be
older than we actually are,

01:41:18.344 --> 01:41:20.094
kind of phenomenon.

01:41:20.094 --> 01:41:24.213
However, I have to credit,
like, Cartoon Network for this,

01:41:24.213 --> 01:41:26.424
it's an American television station

01:41:26.424 --> 01:41:28.253
that had this thing called Toonami.

01:41:28.253 --> 01:41:29.168
(group agreeing)

01:41:29.168 --> 01:41:31.531
Oh, okay, okay, it's
not like just America.

01:41:31.531 --> 01:41:34.325
That was phenomenal, and
Adult Swim was amazing.

01:41:34.325 --> 01:41:37.274
Because they would actually
show like Cowboy Bebop.

01:41:37.274 --> 01:41:40.211
And yeah, what was another?

01:41:40.211 --> 01:41:42.050
