01:50:45.154 --> 01:50:47.401
- You know, I do like hosting.

01:50:47.401 --> 01:50:50.890
I think that is really
where I trained the most in,

01:50:50.890 --> 01:50:52.765
so to speak, and I'm the most comfortable

01:50:52.765 --> 01:50:54.787
being, like, told what to say,

01:50:54.787 --> 01:50:55.965
but also have an opinion about it.

01:50:55.965 --> 01:50:57.805
- Because you're in a weird position

01:50:57.805 --> 01:51:00.865
where it's like, people
know you as a YouTuber--

01:51:00.865 --> 01:51:01.775
- [Reina] I know, right?

01:51:01.775 --> 01:51:04.385
- But you don't really consider
yourself a YouTuber, right?

01:51:04.385 --> 01:51:06.174
- I mean, it's not like a bad thing.

01:51:06.174 --> 01:51:07.275
- Dirty word.

01:51:07.275 --> 01:51:08.536
(guys laughing)

01:51:08.536 --> 01:51:09.787
- I'm not a YouTuber! (laughs)

01:51:09.787 --> 01:51:13.656
- Did you just call me
a content creator? Ew!

01:51:13.656 --> 01:51:15.778
- I mean, in a way, I actually think

01:51:15.778 --> 01:51:18.635
it's more impressive to be a YouTuber,

01:51:18.635 --> 01:51:21.268
where I really wanted to be that

01:51:21.268 --> 01:51:23.568
instead of a host that's hired for stuff.

01:51:23.568 --> 01:51:25.486
- I don't know, man, I think
a host looks way more like--

01:51:25.486 --> 01:51:27.309
- Really? I mean, I can't tell anymore.

01:51:27.309 --> 01:51:28.537
- "Whoa, that's cool."

01:51:28.537 --> 01:51:29.756
- Yeah, it's kind of hard to tell.

01:51:29.756 --> 01:51:31.077
- I feel like it's my mood on the day.

01:51:31.077 --> 01:51:32.458
- Grass is greener, maybe, too?

01:51:32.458 --> 01:51:34.806
- Like, damn, consistent employment?

01:51:34.806 --> 01:51:35.726
That must be nice.

01:51:35.726 --> 01:51:36.559
- Right.

01:51:36.559 --> 01:51:40.368
- But then I guess your earnings
are capped at some point.

01:51:40.368 --> 01:51:41.201
(all agreeing)

01:51:41.201 --> 01:51:43.668
- And your growth potential
is definitely limited.

01:51:43.668 --> 01:51:44.956
(all agreeing)

01:51:44.956 --> 01:51:48.207
But, I do miss working
with a technical team.

01:51:48.207 --> 01:51:50.207
I miss having a co-host.

01:51:51.349 --> 01:51:54.349
And, I guess, I miss a
professional aspect of it.

01:51:54.349 --> 01:51:56.377
Although it's not like
YouTube isn't professional,

01:51:56.377 --> 01:51:58.556
it's just having to take care of

01:51:58.556 --> 01:51:59.907
every aspect of it yourself,

01:51:59.907 --> 01:52:01.268
and then if it comes crashing down,

01:52:01.268 --> 01:52:02.679
it crashes down on you and you implode.

01:52:02.679 --> 01:52:03.512
(guys humming in agreement)

01:52:03.512 --> 01:52:04.345
That's really frightening!

01:52:04.345 --> 01:52:06.054
- It is super nice just
being able to turn up

01:52:06.054 --> 01:52:07.827
and then just do the thing and leave.

01:52:07.827 --> 01:52:08.826
- Right?
- That's pretty good.

01:52:08.826 --> 01:52:10.636
- Someone else does
everything else for you.

01:52:10.636 --> 01:52:14.986
- I feel like really quite
technologically current, right?

01:52:14.986 --> 01:52:17.626
But, even streaming for me,

01:52:17.626 --> 01:52:19.814
it's, like, confusing at times.

01:52:19.814 --> 01:52:20.967
(group agreeing)

01:52:20.967 --> 01:52:23.165
Just having to set up and having to learn,

01:52:23.165 --> 01:52:25.331
especially looking at Connor's set up,

01:52:25.331 --> 01:52:26.745
which Connor says it's easy,

01:52:26.745 --> 01:52:28.574
I'm gonna be like, "No, it's not easy."

01:52:28.574 --> 01:52:30.333
- I know, he said it before,
like, "You could do it too."

01:52:30.333 --> 01:52:31.595
I'm like, "Okay."

01:52:31.595 --> 01:52:33.937
- Well, okay, there's
ways I can dumb it down,

01:52:33.937 --> 01:52:35.531
take away some things that you don't need,

01:52:35.531 --> 01:52:37.356
like all the live sound effects.

01:52:37.356 --> 01:52:39.404
- You need to bare bones that shit.

01:52:39.404 --> 01:52:41.443
- Literally, the stream deck alone

01:52:41.443 --> 01:52:42.949
will up the quality of your stream,

01:52:42.949 --> 01:52:44.268
which is like this tiny little thing,

01:52:44.268 --> 01:52:45.626
with, like, 12 buttons.

01:52:45.626 --> 01:52:47.509
And they all just change
things or play sounds

01:52:47.509 --> 01:52:48.342
or do certain things.

01:52:48.342 --> 01:52:51.493
And it makes it so much more professional.

01:52:51.493 --> 01:52:53.057
And makes it so much easier.

01:52:53.057 --> 01:52:55.428
Because I used to have
to pull up the software,

01:52:55.428 --> 01:52:56.601
scroll to the thing I wanted to click,

01:52:56.601 --> 01:52:58.078
and then change it to the screen.

01:52:58.078 --> 01:53:00.929
So, if I want to be like,
"Okay, show all of my face."

01:53:00.929 --> 01:53:02.108
All right, scroll.

01:53:02.108 --> 01:53:04.299
Oh, I actually want to change
back to the game now, scroll.

01:53:04.299 --> 01:53:05.608
But now it's just, like,
press the buttons on the side.

01:53:05.608 --> 01:53:06.978
(Reina humming in agreement)

01:53:06.978 --> 01:53:08.350
- But there's also times where, you know,

01:53:08.350 --> 01:53:11.400
with this kind of set up, for some reason,

01:53:11.400 --> 01:53:13.453
you change one setting or something,

01:53:13.453 --> 01:53:15.790
you change one setting you
don't remember you did,

01:53:15.790 --> 01:53:18.172
and for some reason,
the sound from your game

01:53:18.172 --> 01:53:20.701
or the sound from the chat
is just not coming out.

01:53:20.701 --> 01:53:22.917
- There's always a technical
issue somewhere, yeah.

01:53:22.917 --> 01:53:24.274
- And you just have to go
through this to-do list

01:53:24.274 --> 01:53:25.608
where you're just checking,

01:53:25.608 --> 01:53:27.102
"okay, is this setting correct?

01:53:27.102 --> 01:53:28.060
"is that setting correct?

01:53:28.060 --> 01:53:29.877
"I don't event remember what I did

01:53:29.877 --> 01:53:31.835
"to set this up to begin with."

01:53:31.835 --> 01:53:33.353
It just adds a layer of complexity.

01:53:33.353 --> 01:53:34.393
(group agreeing)

01:53:34.393 --> 01:53:35.374
- I do think that there's

01:53:35.374 --> 01:53:37.165
such a forgiveness in streaming, right?

01:53:37.165 --> 01:53:38.936
Like, anybody that is your
fan, that's watching you,

01:53:38.936 --> 01:53:41.513
I think they find it charming

01:53:41.513 --> 01:53:43.870
that you have to, not like fumble around,

01:53:43.870 --> 01:53:46.004
but it's very real, to be like,

01:53:46.004 --> 01:53:47.712
"Oh, sorry, like, technical
error, lemme fix it."

01:53:47.712 --> 01:53:49.646
And you're kinda there for the journey.

01:53:49.646 --> 01:53:51.485
- I guess that's kinda like
the bittersweet moment, right?

01:53:51.485 --> 01:53:53.255
'Cause there have been some
moments where I'm like,

01:53:53.255 --> 01:53:54.986
"There is something wrong with my stream,

01:53:54.986 --> 01:53:58.071
"and I cannot for the life
of me fucking figure it out."

01:53:58.071 --> 01:53:59.678
- I just completely forgot something.

01:53:59.678 --> 01:54:02.329
- But, it's kind of nice to be like,

01:54:02.329 --> 01:54:03.218
"Oh, fuck, sorry guys!

01:54:03.218 --> 01:54:04.699
"I'm trying to fix this thing,

01:54:04.699 --> 01:54:05.848
I don't know what the fuck it is,

01:54:05.848 --> 01:54:07.819
I don't want to end the stream,
'cause we just started."

01:54:07.819 --> 01:54:08.809
(group agreeing)

01:54:08.809 --> 01:54:09.859
and this is, like, hundreds
of people being like,

01:54:09.859 --> 01:54:11.698
"It's all good, bro. We'll wait!"

01:54:11.698 --> 01:54:12.849
- Yeah! It's charming!

01:54:12.849 --> 01:54:14.489
Like, that's so sweet.

01:54:14.489 --> 01:54:15.417
- It feels so bad.

01:54:15.417 --> 01:54:17.298
- I don't know, 'cause I get that,

01:54:17.298 --> 01:54:18.848
because a lot of people

01:54:18.848 --> 01:54:20.106
in the comments section are supportive

01:54:20.106 --> 01:54:23.113
but then you start going
through technical difficulties

01:54:23.113 --> 01:54:24.963
and then you see that
live viewer count drop,

01:54:24.963 --> 01:54:26.657
and it just never feels good.

01:54:26.657 --> 01:54:28.054
- If it's something little, it's whatever.

01:54:28.054 --> 01:54:30.102
But if it's, like, stream crashing worthy,

01:54:30.102 --> 01:54:31.483
it's very stressful.

01:54:31.483 --> 01:54:32.446
(all agreeing)

01:54:32.446 --> 01:54:35.212
I accidentally shared my YouTube, like,

01:54:35.212 --> 01:54:39.024
all my analytics one time
stream for like a second.

01:54:39.024 --> 01:54:40.960
- You just accidentally hit the wrong tab?

01:54:40.960 --> 01:54:42.521
- Yeah, I accidentally
shared the wrong thing

01:54:42.521 --> 01:54:43.354
and I was, like,

01:54:43.354 --> 01:54:46.026
"Yeah, guys, that's how much
I made this month, all right?"

01:54:46.026 --> 01:54:46.859
- Fucking hell.

01:54:46.859 --> 01:54:49.243
- I've done worse than that.

01:54:49.243 --> 01:54:50.719
I, okay, so

01:54:50.719 --> 01:54:52.967
I leaked the Trash Taste special.

01:54:52.967 --> 01:54:55.080
- Oh, that's not bad.

01:54:55.080 --> 01:54:57.188
- I've leaked my IP address.

01:54:57.188 --> 01:54:58.376
- Ohhhh!

01:54:58.376 --> 01:54:59.638
- Which is awful.

01:54:59.638 --> 01:55:04.305
That was just the most stressful
realization of my life.

01:55:05.539 --> 01:55:06.412
- Are we getting DDoS'd?

01:55:06.412 --> 01:55:07.465
Are we getting DDoS'd?

01:55:07.465 --> 01:55:09.257
- Like, instant sinking feeling

01:55:09.257 --> 01:55:11.299
to be like, "Okay, I got
to fucking sort this out."

01:55:11.299 --> 01:55:14.516
I literally unplugged my
internet, unplugged everything.

01:55:14.516 --> 01:55:17.915
I googled, "How do I
change my IP address?"

01:55:17.915 --> 01:55:18.938
- Fucking hell.

01:55:18.938 --> 01:55:22.355
- Yeah, basically, don't test your speed.

01:55:23.997 --> 01:55:25.924
Don't test your speed live on stream.

01:55:25.924 --> 01:55:27.923
(group groaning)

01:55:27.923 --> 01:55:31.159
I didn't realize my IP
address was right there.

01:55:31.159 --> 01:55:32.192
- How did you save it?

01:55:32.192 --> 01:55:34.033
What did you do when you shared it?

01:55:34.033 --> 01:55:36.694
- Luckily, luckily it
wasn't that complicated.

01:55:36.694 --> 01:55:37.574
'Cause I googled it.

01:55:37.574 --> 01:55:39.972
All you have to do, 'cause I
don't have a static IP address,

01:55:39.972 --> 01:55:43.092
all I had to do was unplug
my router, plug it in again.

01:55:43.092 --> 01:55:45.150
But, I don't know, at the
time, I was just like,

01:55:45.150 --> 01:55:47.184
"Well, my Internet's fucked!"

01:55:47.184 --> 01:55:49.973
- Yeah, I feel like, how
you handle the fuck up,

01:55:49.973 --> 01:55:51.735
is like the most important part.

01:55:51.735 --> 01:55:55.390
When I flashed my thing, I'm
like, "You know what, guys?

01:55:55.390 --> 01:55:56.704
"I'll just fucking show
you, just have a look."

01:55:56.704 --> 01:55:57.826
- You owned it.

01:55:57.826 --> 01:56:00.309
- "You're gonna look at the
clip, just have a look."

01:56:00.309 --> 01:56:01.142
And then I was like,

01:56:01.142 --> 01:56:02.892
"All right, so I know
it seems like a lot."

01:56:02.892 --> 01:56:04.788
(all laughing)

01:56:04.788 --> 01:56:06.601
- It's just an estimate!

01:56:06.601 --> 01:56:07.788
- YouTube takes 40%.

01:56:07.788 --> 01:56:09.488
- You know, YouTube takes a cut.

01:56:09.488 --> 01:56:11.130
There's a lot of costs involved.

01:56:11.130 --> 01:56:13.321
It's real easy to look at that number.

01:56:13.321 --> 01:56:15.904
(all laughing)

01:56:17.321 --> 01:56:18.444
- Just fucking sweating.

01:56:18.444 --> 01:56:20.749
- I'm like, "You know, tax is like 40%!"

01:56:20.749 --> 01:56:22.771
You know, it's pretty brutal.

01:56:22.771 --> 01:56:25.041
- So, basically, I see none of it.

01:56:25.041 --> 01:56:26.170
(all laughing)

01:56:26.170 --> 01:56:27.180
- "What I'm trying to say is, 'I'm broke.'

01:56:27.180 --> 01:56:30.105
"Thanks for the $10 donation,
by the way, Tim in the chat."

01:56:30.105 --> 01:56:31.412
I'm kidding.

01:56:31.412 --> 01:56:33.461
Well, that's what I tell
people when I'm streaming.

01:56:33.461 --> 01:56:34.762
I don't stream 'cause like,

01:56:34.762 --> 01:56:36.402
some people do it 'cause they're like,

01:56:36.402 --> 01:56:37.731
"I want to get more subs."

01:56:37.731 --> 01:56:38.921
I just do it 'cause I
like playing the game,

01:56:38.921 --> 01:56:40.541
I don't like playing games alone anymore.

01:56:40.541 --> 01:56:42.207
(guys humming in agreement)
For me, I don't know why,

01:56:42.207 --> 01:56:43.040
I think that's probably a bad thing,

01:56:43.040 --> 01:56:44.612
that I've ruined gaming alone for myself.

01:56:44.612 --> 01:56:45.445
- [Garnt] Right.

01:56:45.445 --> 01:56:47.126
- I only like gaming with an audience now.

01:56:47.126 --> 01:56:48.104
I don't know what that says about me,

01:56:48.104 --> 01:56:49.924
what's wrong with me mentally.

01:56:49.924 --> 01:56:51.389
- That's like literally the only thing

01:56:51.389 --> 01:56:53.875
that's stopping me from
fully committing to Twitch.

01:56:53.875 --> 01:56:56.885
Is the fact that I don't want
another one of my hobbies

01:56:56.885 --> 01:56:57.953
to turn into a job.

01:56:57.953 --> 01:56:59.715
- I completely understand, yes!

01:56:59.715 --> 01:57:01.845
That's also my other reason.

01:57:01.845 --> 01:57:03.630
- I was falling out of love with gaming

01:57:03.630 --> 01:57:05.410
and I think Twitch really saved it for me.

01:57:05.410 --> 01:57:06.243
(group humming in agreement)

01:57:06.243 --> 01:57:07.107
and that's why when I'm
streaming more, it's like,

01:57:07.107 --> 01:57:08.314
"Yeah, dude, you can sub if you want,

01:57:08.314 --> 01:57:09.783
"but I really don't care.

01:57:09.783 --> 01:57:13.712
"You don't need to, I'm
doing this regardless."

01:57:13.712 --> 01:57:15.836
And I just hope people
believe me when I say that.

01:57:15.836 --> 01:57:16.969
It's so easy to sound like bullshit

01:57:16.969 --> 01:57:18.635
when you say stuff like that.
- [Joey] Yeah, of course.

01:57:18.635 --> 01:57:21.293
- Try to justify why you have
like 30K revenue last month,

01:57:21.293 --> 01:57:23.699
you're like, "Oh my god, um."

01:57:23.699 --> 01:57:26.588
- You should've just been
like, "I don't choose the CPM."

01:57:26.588 --> 01:57:27.549
(all laughing)

01:57:27.549 --> 01:57:30.418
- I'm like, you know, it used
to be, like, I couldn't live.

01:57:30.418 --> 01:57:32.560
And now I live comfortably, you know.

01:57:32.560 --> 01:57:34.371
It's, like, things change, you know.

01:57:34.371 --> 01:57:35.640
(all laughing)

01:57:35.640 --> 01:57:37.957
I'm like sinking in my
chair, like, "Fuck!"

01:57:37.957 --> 01:57:41.159
- I can't believe you wanted
to justify, that's so scary.

01:57:41.159 --> 01:57:42.358
I would've just like cut the whole stream.

01:57:42.358 --> 01:57:44.628
I would've been like, "That
was a technical error!"

01:57:44.628 --> 01:57:45.678
"Somebody hacked me!"

01:57:45.678 --> 01:57:46.511
(group agreeing)

01:57:46.511 --> 01:57:48.325
- Damn, Photoshop is advanced these days!

01:57:48.325 --> 01:57:51.065
Wow, I Photoshopped my
own analytics, damn.

01:57:51.065 --> 01:57:52.022
Would you look at that?

01:57:52.022 --> 01:57:54.594
- You shoulda just opened up
Paint and just drawn a three.

01:57:54.594 --> 01:57:55.851
Been like, "Oh, no!"

01:57:55.851 --> 01:57:58.824
- Just like erase one of the zeroes.

01:57:58.824 --> 01:58:00.240
- I think people know, though.

01:58:00.240 --> 01:58:02.112
I think, you know, when
you get to a certain size,

01:58:02.112 --> 01:58:03.945
people are like, "I expect
you to make some money."

01:58:03.945 --> 01:58:04.778
You know?

01:58:04.778 --> 01:58:05.611
(group agreeing)

01:58:05.611 --> 01:58:06.444
It always feels weird,

01:58:06.444 --> 01:58:07.277
'cause I feel like I don't deserve it.

01:58:07.277 --> 01:58:08.912
- Well they're estimates
are also, like, way off.

01:58:08.912 --> 01:58:09.831
- Yeah, they are, they are.

01:58:09.831 --> 01:58:10.830
- [Garnt] Yeah, they are.

01:58:10.830 --> 01:58:12.711
- Someone's like, "You
probably make like $500,000."

01:58:12.711 --> 01:58:14.671
I'm like, "Are you fucking stupid?"

01:58:14.671 --> 01:58:17.913
- It is so hilarious looking
up fucking websites being like,

01:58:17.913 --> 01:58:20.183
"The Anime Man's net worth!"

01:58:20.183 --> 01:58:21.305
- [Connor] Ten million dollars.

01:58:21.305 --> 01:58:23.375
- It's always like ten times more

01:58:23.375 --> 01:58:24.523
than what you actually make.

01:58:24.523 --> 01:58:26.745
- Because it's an estimate, right?

01:58:26.745 --> 01:58:27.623
- The range!

01:58:27.623 --> 01:58:29.415
- The range is fucking hilarious.

01:58:29.415 --> 01:58:31.493
- It's like, "The Anime Man
is worth anywhere between

01:58:31.493 --> 01:58:34.023
"$200,000 to $10 million."

01:58:34.023 --> 01:58:37.002
I'm like, "I'm sure I
am somewhere in there!"

01:58:37.002 --> 01:58:39.074
- [Reina] Somewhere!
- I mean, I do get it.

01:58:39.074 --> 01:58:41.455
Now, that I'm a YouTuber,
'cause for the longest time,

01:58:41.455 --> 01:58:43.214
I thought how much I earned

01:58:43.214 --> 01:58:45.483
is how much everyone's earned, or like it.

01:58:45.483 --> 01:58:49.053
And I've only recently realized,
"Man, CPM fucking matters."

01:58:49.053 --> 01:58:49.886
(group agreeing)

01:58:49.886 --> 01:58:50.783
- [Reina] What country.

01:58:50.783 --> 01:58:52.574
- The subject matter that you talk about

01:58:52.574 --> 01:58:53.483
also fucking matters.

01:58:53.483 --> 01:58:55.062
Like, I will say this,

01:58:55.062 --> 01:58:58.112
as a person who does
anime content on YouTube,

01:58:58.112 --> 01:58:59.923
CPM fucking sucks.

01:58:59.923 --> 01:59:00.756
- Nah, it's shit.

01:59:00.756 --> 01:59:01.674
It's absolute shit.

01:59:01.674 --> 01:59:03.496
- I didn't realize how much other people

01:59:03.496 --> 01:59:05.685
in the like similar size of me,

01:59:05.685 --> 01:59:07.496
was earning in other fields

01:59:07.496 --> 01:59:10.143
until people started exposing
how much they earned.

01:59:10.143 --> 01:59:11.044
- Yeah, exactly.

01:59:11.044 --> 01:59:12.862
- You know, you're so
desperate for a video,

01:59:12.862 --> 01:59:14.763
you're like, "Fuck it, I'll
out myself as a millionaire."

01:59:14.763 --> 01:59:16.514
(all laughing)

01:59:16.514 --> 01:59:18.354
"I'm not one of you guys, I lied!"

